 "independent_report": "# Independent EVD-033 verdict\n\nPASS on the first and only guest launch at frozen revision 9b4207086ea95a1ef46cd891358811ad00d8d324. ELF SHA-256 de6998f732dd148517f04a9087ae096ec24ddca7d0e37aeb170190e12e06afac. Initial CLI invocation exited 2 before spawning QEMU because this revision lacks --capture-dir. The supported --qemu Python launcher hard-linked the observer UART file, then exec'd Ubuntu /usr/bin/qemu-system-aarch64 with -d int and -D. The first guest passed the observer quiet window, exited under host SIGTERM, and was never relaunched. boot.log records the real invocation and PID.\n\nRun python validate.py in any directory to replay the independent byte and exception checks. The 111 raw UART bytes matched exactly. In first-release enqueue order B then A, the jobs have (period,relative deadline) A=(10,9), B=(12,4). RM ran AB at tick zero, DM ran BA. Both epochs dispatched A at tick 10 and B at tick 12. Within each 14-IRQ epoch the eight total SVCs split 2,1,1 after local IRQ 1,11,13. Each final worker completion returned to controller PC 0x40201260 before tick 13. Final IRQ parks after verifying eight completions and empty jobs.\n\nAll 28 IRQs came from controller ELR 0x40201260 via vector 0x40200a80. Initial controller entry was 0x4020124c. IRQ handler 0x40201324 checks GICC_IAR ID 30 and CNTP_CTL_EL0 low bits equal 5. Eight SVC #1 exceptions used vector 0x40200a00 and ESR 0x56000001. Worker A entered 0x40201268 with marker ID 0, called marker 0x402019e8 then trapped at 0x40201274 (ELR 0x40201278). Worker B entered 0x4020127c with marker ID 1 and trapped at 0x40201288 (ELR 0x4020128c). The marker checks the incoming ID and SP. From the ELF, A/B marker SPs are 0x402070c0/0x4020b0c0. Completion at 0x40201b04 checks syndrome and saved frame addresses 0x40206d80/0x4020ad80. Controller stack top 0x4020f0c0 with 16 bytes local and 0x340 frame implies saved address 0x4020ed70. These addresses are derived from executed guest checks. QEMU -d int directly records control-flow PCs and syndrome.\n\nRaw SHA-256 uart.raw ca1b1057d80b4a489eed5a4c2601bfd2c538051921cafad4e17147fca7311bc3 and interrupt.trace 59c27ef7a46bfac2831d25f9adcb341a0589ac676e9df786c5a23e2b1aea2774. elf.disasm is the frozen executable disassembly used for review.\n",
